0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the Intel 8080
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-11-24).
0000                             ;  Design follows the Z80 interpreter (z80/b8s-z80.asm), with 8080 opcodes
0000                             ;  only.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Three switches, set in the EQU lines below:
0000                             ;    CPM      0 = generic ROM build (KEY/CONOUT at fixed addresses)
0000                             ;             1 = CP/M 2.2 .COM file: loads the file named on the command line
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks (spec: the programmer is responsible)
0000                             ;             1 = starts with every variable at 0 and every word undefined,
0000                             ;                 and stops on every error in the spec's table (and Ctrl-C)
0000                             ;                 with a three-line report: the letter and the place as line
0000                             ;                 and column, and both stacks. See `error`.
0000                             ;    ANSI     what the console escapes of "$" (/00bbIC8= /| /` /~) do:
0000                             ;             1 = send ANSI (VT100) sequences through CONOUT
0000                             ;             0 = call the machine's own routines CONCLS, CONEOL, CONCUR and
0000                             ;                 CONAT (see the equates). The CP/M builds always send ANSI.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  In every build Ctrl-C stops a running program (an unchecked build stops
0000                             ;  without a word): see the console layer for the rules, the held key and
0000                             ;  the break-off cell.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80 (https://maly.github.io/asm80-node/), I8080 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CPM:      EQU   1   ; 1 = CP/M .COM build
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   1   ; 1 = checked build
0000                ANSI:     EQU   0   ; 1 = the console escapes send ANSI sequences
0000                ANS:      EQU   ANSI+CPM-ANSI*CPM   ; (CP/M: always ANSI)
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Register use, everywhere in the interpreter
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    BC   IP: the address of the next program character to read
0000                             ;    HL   TOS: the top data-stack cell is kept here, not in memory
0000                             ;    SP   the data stack: (SP) is NOS, the cell under TOS. The data stack is
0000                             ;         the 8080"s own stack, which is what the spec"s machine-code contract
0000                             ;         needs ("the data cells above the return address").
0000                             ;    A DE scratch. Every handler is entered with HL = TOS and may use A, DE.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The return stack pointer has no register (the 8080 has no spare pair): it
0000                             ;  is the RAM word RSP. Only rpop, rpushd and ")" (and the checks) touch it.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  One-byte calls. In a generic build the routines used most are reached
0000                             ;  with RST, one byte instead of three. The source writes them as macros:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    POPR   RST 1  08h  rpop    pop the return stack into HL
0000                             ;    DROP   RST 3  18h  drp     drop TOS, then next character  (ends a handler)
0000                             ;    NEGH   RST 4  20h  neg16   HL = -HL
0000                             ;    PUTA   RST 5  28h  putc    print A
0000                             ;    NEXT   RST 6  30h  next0   next character                 (ends a handler)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  RST 3 and RST 6 never return: an RST is a CALL, so the first thing each
0000                             ;  of them does is POP D to throw the return address away.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  A CP/M build leaves page zero alone (CP/M keeps it for interrupts, and
0000                             ;  RomWBW's BIOS calls itself through RST 1): there the macros are CALLs, and
0000                             ;  DROP and NEXT are JMPs.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch. PTAB holds one byte per punctuation character: the low byte of
0000                             ;  its handler's address. The high byte is worked out from the character:
0000                             ;  the handlers of the first NPG1 characters (in code order) start in the
0000                             ;  image's second page, the rest in its first. The layout below keeps to
0000                             ;  that, and testing/chktab.py checks it in every build.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  What the 8080 lacks, and what replaces it: no JR (JMP/Jcc), no DJNZ, no
0000                             ;  SBC HL (byte-wise SUB/SBB, or negate and DAD), no shifts on register pairs
0000                             ;  (DAD H doubles; RAL/RAR through A), no LDIR/CPIR (small loops).
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map. Everything the interpreter writes is in four RAM pages:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RSPAGE   return stack, 112 entries (the pointer stays inside this page)
0000                             ;    DSPAGE   data stack, 127 cells (the top four bytes of the page are spare,
0000                             ;             so a full stack runs two bytes into the page below)
0000                             ;    LETPAGE  letter cells: A..Z at +00h..+33h, a..z at +40h..+73h (so a word
0000                             ;             cell is always 64 bytes below its variable), the heap pointer at
0000                             ;             +7Ch, interpreter variables in the gaps, and the -n? line buffer
0000                             ;             at +80h..+FFh
0000                             ;    PROG     the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap starts after the NUL
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the single range from the letter
0000                             ;  page up to the heap limit. Each stack has a guard band: the data stack can
0000                             ;  overrun by a cell or two (and the calls made while it is full, the error
0000                             ;  report's included) into the top 32 bytes of the return-stack page, which
0000                             ;  are never used, and the return stack by one entry into the page below it.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                          IF   CPM   
0000                BDOS:     EQU   0005h   
0000                EXIT:     EQU   0000h   ; warm boot
0000                BASE:     EQU   0100h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IFN   CPM   
                                 ; ---- generic machine: edit these to suit -----------------------------------
                    KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
                                 ;   waiting. The zero flag must match A
                                 ;   (end the routine with ORA A / RET).
                    CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
                    EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
                                 ;   KEY and CONOUT must preserve BC, DE and HL.
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   1-ANS   
                                 ; With ANSI = 0 the console escapes call these. All four must keep BC, and
                                 ; all but CONAT also HL. They may change A, DE and the flags.
                    CONCLS:   EQU   0FF0Ch   ; /{  clear the screen, the cursor to the top left
                    CONEOL:   EQU   0FF0Fh   ; /}  clear from the cursor to the end of the line
                    CONCUR:   EQU   0FF12h   ; /| and /`  show the cursor if A is not 0, hide
                                 ;     it if A = 0
                    CONAT:    EQU   0FF15h   ; /~  the cursor to row HL, column DE, both
                                 ;     counted from 0. May change A, DE and HL
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IFN   CPM   
                    RSPAGE:   EQU   80h   ; 8000h return stack
                    DSPAGE:   EQU   81h   ; 8100h data stack
                    LETPAGE:   EQU   82h   ; 8200h letter cells and line buffer
                    PROG:     EQU   8300h   ; where the loader puts the program text
                    HEAPLIM:   EQU   0F0h   ; the heap must stay below F000h (a page)
                    BASE:     EQU   0000h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   40-36*CPM   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms (1-255;
0000                             ; the wait for a second Ctrl-C uses it too):
0000                             ; each pass calls getk once, so tune it for
0000                             ; your clock and your KEY routine. CP/M: 4,
0000                             ; for a BDOS 6 call of about 280 us (an RC2014
0000                             ; with RomWBW and ZPM3). A .COM can be
0000                             ; patched: see TIMING.B8S.
0000                             ; letter-page layout (offsets inside LETPAGE)
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                HEAP:     EQU   LET+7Ch   ; the heap pointer
0000                RSP:      EQU   LET+34h   ; gap after Z: the return stack pointer;
0000                BRKCNT:   EQU   LET+36h   ;   the break check's countdown;
0000                NPEND:    EQU   LET+38h   ;   minus the address of the program's end
0000                             ;   (the heap"s first byte), for the checked "_';
0000                PSAVE:    EQU   LET+3Ah   ;   the checked build: the address "$" prints
0000                             ;   from, for a report
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   LET+7Ah   ; gap after z: a key read by the break check and
0000                             ;   held for the next "?" (0: none);
0000                BRKOFF:   EQU   LET+7Bh   ;   the break-off cell: a program that stores a
0000                             ;   non-zero byte here gets Ctrl-C as a key
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSTOP:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+0E0h   ; empty return stack: the 32 bytes above it
0000                             ; take calls made while the data stack is full
0000                DSTOP:    EQU   DSPAGE*256+0FCh   ; empty data stack. The four bytes above it
0000                             ; are spare: a character can pop two cells
0000                             ; too many before the checked build sees it,
0000                             ; and the next call must not land on the
0000                             ; letter cells.
0000                             ; The five one-byte calls (see the header). asm80 can't nest IF, so these
0000                             ; are written with DS: a count of 0 writes nothing. DS can't take a label
0000                             ; that comes later, but EQU can, and DS can take that.
0000                AROP:     EQU   rpop   
0000                ADRP:     EQU   drp   
0000                ANEG:     EQU   neg16   
0000                APUT:     EQU   putc   
0000                ANXT:     EQU   next0   
0000                .macro POPR,
0000                             ; 
0000                 DS      1-CPM,0CFh      ;   RST 1
0000                 DS      CPM,0CDh        ;   CALL rpop
0000                 DS      CPM,AROP&0FFh
0000                 DS      CPM,AROP/256
0000                .endm
0000                 
0000                .macro DROP,
0000                             ; 
0000                 DS      1-CPM,0DFh      ;   RST 3
0000                 DS      CPM,0C3h        ;   JMP drp
0000                 DS      CPM,ADRP&0FFh
0000                 DS      CPM,ADRP/256
0000                .endm
0000                 
0000                .macro NEGH,
0000                             ; 
0000                 DS      1-CPM,0E7h      ;   RST 4
0000                 DS      CPM,0CDh        ;   CALL neg16
0000                 DS      CPM,ANEG&0FFh
0000                 DS      CPM,ANEG/256
0000                .endm
0000                 
0000                .macro PUTA,
0000                             ; 
0000                 DS      1-CPM,0EFh      ;   RST 5
0000                 DS      CPM,0CDh        ;   CALL putc
0000                 DS      CPM,APUT&0FFh
0000                 DS      CPM,APUT/256
0000                .endm
0000                 
0000                .macro NEXT,
0000                             ; 
0000                 DS      1-CPM,0F7h      ;   RST 6
0000                 DS      CPM,0C3h        ;   JMP next0
0000                 DS      CPM,ANXT&0FFh
0000                 DS      CPM,ANXT/256
0000                .endm
0000                 
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  The first 49 bytes: the entry, then the RST routines, with small handlers
0000                             ;  and routines filling the gaps between them. Generic: this IS page zero.
0000                             ;  CP/M: it is just the start of the .COM file.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0100                          .ORG   BASE   
0100                          IF   1-(1-CPM)*CHECKED   
0100   31 FC 09               LXI   SP,DSTOP   ; 00  reset, or the start of the .COM file
0103                          ENDIF      
0103   C3 E8 06               JMP   start   ; In the checked generic build this is at 0000h
0106                             ;   (and `start` sets SP): its first byte, C3h,
0106                             ;   is what an undefined word runs into, as
0106                             ;   CP/M's own JMP at 0000h is in a .COM: e_hi.
0106                          IF   (1-CPM)*CHECKED   
                              DB   0,0,0   ; 03  spare
0106                          ENDIF      
0106                          ;*Macro unroll: rdrop:  POPR                    ; 06  drop the top of the return stack, then
0106                RDROP:    DS   1-CPM,0CFh   ; 06  drop the top of the return stack, then
0106   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
0107   0C                     DS   CPM,AROP&0FFh   
0108   01                     DS   CPM,AROP/256   
0109                          ;*Macro unroll:  DROP                    ;     drop TOS (a spent flag) and go on
0109                          DS   1-CPM,0DFh   ;     drop TOS (a spent flag) and go on
0109   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
010A   1C                     DS   CPM,ADRP&0FFh   
010B   01                     DS   CPM,ADRP/256   
010C                             ; ---- RST 1: rpop: pop the return stack into HL (DE is lost) -----------------
010C   2A 34 0A     RPOP:     LHLD   RSP   ; 08
010F   5E                     MOV   E,M   
0110   23                     INX   H   
0111   56                     MOV   D,M   
0112   23                     INX   H   
0113   22 34 0A               SHLD   RSP   
0116   EB                     XCHG      
0117   C9                     RET      ; 13  (so RST 2 is not used)
0118   EB           H_TOR:    XCHG      ; 14  "{" TOS to the return stack; rpushd
0119   C3 3B 05               JMP   rpushd   ;     brings up the new TOS
011C                             ; ---- RST 3: drop TOS, then next ---------------------------------------------
011C                          IF   1-CPM   
                    RST18:    POP   D   ; 18  discard the RST's return address
011C                          ENDIF      
011C   E1           DRP:      POP   H   ;     new TOS = NOS
011D   C3 36 01               JMP   next0   
0120   E5           H_FROMR:   PUSH   H   ; 1D  "}" return stack to TOS
0121                          ;*Macro unroll:  POPR
0121                          DS   1-CPM,0CFh   
0121   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
0122   0C                     DS   CPM,AROP&0FFh   
0123   01                     DS   CPM,AROP/256   
0124                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
0124                          DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
0124   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
0125   36                     DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
0126   01                     DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
0127                             ; ---- RST 4: neg16: HL = -HL (keeps BC, DE) ----------------------------------
0127   AF           NEG16:    XRA   A   ; 20
0128   95                     SUB   L   
0129   6F                     MOV   L,A   
012A   9F                     SBB   A   
012B   94                     SUB   H   
012C   67                     MOV   H,A   
012D   C9                     RET      
012E   E9           JPHL:     PCHL      ; 27  (for the machine-code call)
012F                             ; ---- RST 5: putc: print A (keeps BC, DE, HL) --------------------------------
012F                          IFN   CPM   
                    RST28:       
                    PUTC:     JMP   CONOUT   ; 28
012F                          ENDIF      
012F                             ; exec: "`" with no hex digit after it: call the machine code at TOS. It
012F                             ; returns here, with its top cell on the stack: that becomes the new TOS.
012F   CD 2E 01     EXEC:     CALL   jphl   ; 2B
0132   E1                     POP   H   
0133                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
0133                          DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
0133   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
0134   36                     DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
0135   01                     DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
0136                             ; ---- RST 6: next character --------------------------------------------------
0136                          IF   1-CPM   
                    RST30:    POP   D   ; 30  discard the RST's return address
0136                          ENDIF      
0136                             ; =============================================================================
0136                             ;  The inner loop: read one character and sort it by range.
0136                             ; 
0136                             ;    00h          end of program
0136                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh-FFh   ignored (control, space, DEL, high bytes)
0136                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
0136                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
0136                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
0136                             ;    the rest     punctuation: jump through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
0136                             ; =============================================================================
0136                NEXT0:       
0136                          IF   CHECKED   
0136   CD C9 05               CALL   chkstk   ; both stacks are checked once per character
0139                          ENDIF      
0139   0A                     LDAX   B   
013A   03                     INX   B   
013B   D6 21                  SUI   21h   ; A = c - 21h
013D   DA 80 01               JC   ctl   ; c < 21h: NUL ends, the rest are ignored
0140   FE 0F                  CPI   0Fh   
0142   DA 70 01               JC   punct   ; 21h-2Fh: PTAB index 0-14
0145   D6 0F                  SUI   0Fh   ; A = c - 30h
0147   FE 0A                  CPI   0Ah   
0149   DA 76 03               JC   digit   ; 30h-39h
014C   FE 11                  CPI   11h   
014E   DA 6E 01               JC   p3a   ; 3Ah-40h
0151   D6 11                  SUI   11h   ; A = c - 41h
0153   FE 1A                  CPI   1Ah   
0155   DA 31 05               JC   upper   ; 41h-5Ah: A = letter index 0-25
0158   FE 20                  CPI   20h   
015A   DA 6C 01               JC   p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
015D   FE 3A                  CPI   3Ah   
015F   DA 29 05               JC   lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h (cell +64 bytes)
0162   FE 3E                  CPI   3Eh   
0164                          IF   CHECKED   
0164   CA 36 01               JZ   next0   ; 7Fh, DEL: ignored
0167   D2 00 06               JNC   e_hi   ; 80h-FFh: reserved
016A                          ENDIF      
016A                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              JNC   next0   ; 7Fh-FFh: ignored
016A                          ENDIF      
016A   D6 1A                  SUI   1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: -1Eh in all, index 28-31
016C   D6 09        P5B:      SUI   9   ; 5Bh-60h: -4 in all, index 22-27
016E   C6 05        P3A:      ADI   5   ; 3Ah-40h: index 15-21
0170                             ; Punctuation: A = the PTAB index. The handler starts with HL = TOS,
0170                             ; untouched, and A, DE free.
0170   C6 56        PUNCT:    ADI   PTAB & 0FFh   ; PTAB never crosses a page
0172   5F                     MOV   E,A   
0173   16 03                  MVI   D,PTAB / 256   
0175   FE 6C                  CPI   (PTAB & 0FFh) + NPG1   ; carry: one of the first NPG1
0177   1A                     LDAX   D   
0178   5F                     MOV   E,A   ; the handler's low byte
0179                          IFN   CPM   
                              MVI   A,0   
                              RAL      ; its page: 0 + carry
0179                          ENDIF      
0179                          IF   CPM   
0179   3E 01                  MVI   A,1   
017B   CE 00                  ACI   0   ; its page: 1 + carry
017D                          ENDIF      
017D   57                     MOV   D,A   
017E   D5                     PUSH   D   ; jump to it; the stack is balanced again
017F   C9                     RET      ;   when the handler starts
0180                             ; ctl: characters below 21h. A = c - 21h.
0180   C6 21        CTL:      ADI   21h   ; back to c; zero only for NUL
0182   C2 36 01               JNZ   next0   ; the rest are ignored
0185   C3 00 00     ENDPROG:   JMP   EXIT   ; the program has ended
0188                             ; =============================================================================
0188                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's first page: ^ _ ` | ~
0188                             ;  (00bbIGFuZCA= are up among the RST routines.)
0188                             ; =============================================================================
0188   D1           H_XOR:    POP   D   
0189   7C                     MOV   A,H   
018A   AA                     XRA   D   
018B   67                     MOV   H,A   
018C   7D                     MOV   A,L   
018D   AB                     XRA   E   
018E   6F                     MOV   L,A   
018F                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
018F                          DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
018F   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
0190   36                     DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
0191   01                     DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
0192   D1           H_OR:     POP   D   
0193   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0194   B2                     ORA   D   
0195   67                     MOV   H,A   
0196   7D                     MOV   A,L   
0197   B3                     ORA   E   
0198   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0199                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
0199                          DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
0199   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
019A   36                     DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
019B   01                     DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
019C                          ;*Macro unroll: h_not:  NEGH                    ; ~x = -x - 1
019C                H_NOT:    DS   1-CPM,0E7h   ; ~x = -x - 1
019C   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
019D   27                     DS   CPM,ANEG&0FFh   
019E   01                     DS   CPM,ANEG/256   
019F   2B                     DCX   H   
01A0                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
01A0                          DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
01A0   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
01A1   36                     DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
01A2   01                     DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
01A3                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap pointer moves by n, a signed count (the add is
01A3                             ; the same either way); TOS is the old pointer.
01A3   EB           H_ALLOC:   XCHG      
01A4   2A 7C 0A               LHLD   HEAP   
01A7   E5                     PUSH   H   
01A8   19                     DAD   D   ; the new top
01A9                          IF   CHECKED   
01A9   CD 60 05               CALL   chkhp   
01AC                          ENDIF      
01AC   22 7C 0A               SHLD   HEAP   
01AF   E1                     POP   H   
01B0                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
01B0                          DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
01B0   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
01B1   36                     DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
01B2   01                     DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
01B3                          IF   1-CPM   
                                 ; ---- the letters and digits --------------------------------------------------
                                 ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
                    LOWER:    PUSH   H   
                              ADD   A   
                              MOV   L,A   
                              MVI   H,LETPAGE   
                              ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
                              DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
                              DS   CPM,0C3h   
                              DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
                              DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
                                 ; A-Z: call the word. The return address (the IP after the letter) goes on
                                 ; the return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
                    UPPER:    PUSH   H   ; keep TOS: rpushd pops it back
                              ADD   A   
                              MOV   L,A   
                              MVI   H,LETPAGE   ; HL -> cell
                              MOV   D,B   
                              MOV   E,C   ; DE = the return address
                              MOV   C,M   
                              INX   H   
                              MOV   B,M   ; IP = the word's body, and fall into rpushd
                                 ; rpushd: push DE on the return stack, then pop TOS off the data stack and
                                 ; go on. Every push of the return stack ends here: for a word call the cell
                                 ; popped is the TOS that upper parked; for "(" and "{" it is the cell under
                                 ; the one that was used up.
                                 ; 
                                 ; The break key is looked at here, so at every word call and loop-back (and
                                 ; block entry and "{"), but only one time in 256: BRKCNT counts them. Reading
                                 ; the keyboard can be slow (it is a BDOS call under CP/M).
                    RPUSHD:   LHLD   RSP   
                              DCX   H   
                              MOV   M,D   
                              DCX   H   
                              MOV   M,E   
                              SHLD   RSP   
                              LXI   H,BRKCNT   
                              DCR   M   
                              POP   H   ; (keeps the flags)
                              CZ   pollk   
                              ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
                              DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
                              DS   CPM,0C3h   
                              DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
                              DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
01B3                          ENDIF      
01B3                             ; ---- machine code: the grave -----------------------------------------------
01B3                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
01B3                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RET (C9h) is
01B3                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
01B3                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ). The
01B3                             ; code is entered by CALL with the data stack above the return address; it
01B3                             ; must keep BC, and on return the top cell becomes the new TOS.
01B3   CD D3 04     H_GRAVE:   CALL   hexc   
01B6   D2 2F 01               JNC   exec   
01B9   87           HX1:      ADD   A   
01BA   87                     ADD   A   
01BB   87                     ADD   A   
01BC   87                     ADD   A   
01BD   57                     MOV   D,A   ; the high digit
01BE   CD D3 04               CALL   hexc   
01C1   D2 CD 01               JNC   hx2   ; odd digit: consumed and dropped
01C4   B2                     ORA   D   
01C5   77                     MOV   M,A   
01C6   23                     INX   H   
01C7   CD D3 04               CALL   hexc   
01CA   DA B9 01               JC   hx1   
01CD   36 C9        HX2:      MVI   M,0C9h   ; (never range-checked: the spec says so)
01CF                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
01CF                          DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
01CF   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
01D0   36                     DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
01D1   01                     DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
01D2                             ; ---- where the two pages meet ----------------------------------------------
01D2                             ; The first page ends somewhere among the next four handlers, ] \ [ @ (they
01D2                             ; are in falling code order for this), and where exactly differs between the
01D2                             ; builds: NPG1 follows. Every handler below these four must start in the
01D2                             ; second page, and every one above in the first; chktab.py checks both.
01D2                             ; "]" returns: pop an address and jump to it. TOS is parked on the stack
01D2                             ; while rpop uses HL, and the drop at the end brings it back.
01D2   E5           H_RET:    PUSH   H   
01D3                          ;*Macro unroll: ret2:   POPR
01D3                RET2:     DS   1-CPM,0CFh   
01D3   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
01D4   0C                     DS   CPM,AROP&0FFh   
01D5   01                     DS   CPM,AROP/256   
01D6   44                     MOV   B,H   
01D7   4D                     MOV   C,L   
01D8                          ;*Macro unroll:  DROP
01D8                          DS   1-CPM,0DFh   
01D8   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
01D9   1C                     DS   CPM,ADRP&0FFh   
01DA   01                     DS   CPM,ADRP/256   
01DB                             ; "\" ( flag -- ): true skips to the next ")" or "]" at this level; ")"
01DB                             ; drops the block start, "]" returns. No closer at all ends the program.
01DB                             ; The flag stays in HL as the spent cell that rdrop and ret2 drop.
01DB   7C           H_BREAK:   MOV   A,H   
01DC   B5                     ORA   L   
01DD   CA EB 02               JZ   h_drop   ; false: just drop the flag
01E0   CD 7C 04               CALL   skip   
01E3   B7                     ORA   A   ; skip returns 0 for ")"
01E4   C2 D3 01               JNZ   ret2   
01E7   C3 06 01               JMP   rdrop   
01EA                             ; "[" followed by a letter stores the body"s address in that letter"s cell:
01EA                             ; uppercase is a word, lowercase a variable. Followed by a space it pushes
01EA                             ; the body"s address instead. Either way it then skips to the matching "]'.
01EA                             ; (The unchecked build takes anything that is not a letter as the space; the
01EA                             ; checked build stops on it.)
01EA   0A           H_DEF:    LDAX   B   
01EB   03                     INX   B   
01EC   D6 41                  SUI   "A"   ; a letter gives 0-25 or 32-57: lowercase
01EE   5F                     MOV   E,A   ;   lands 64 bytes up
01EF   E6 DF                  ANI   0DFh   ; fold case
01F1   FE 1A                  CPI   26   
01F3   D2 03 02               JNC   def2   ; not a letter
01F6   7B                     MOV   A,E   
01F7   87                     ADD   A   
01F8   5F                     MOV   E,A   
01F9   16 0A                  MVI   D,LETPAGE   ; DE -> cell
01FB   79                     MOV   A,C   
01FC   12                     STAX   D   
01FD   1C                     INR   E   
01FE   78                     MOV   A,B   
01FF   12                     STAX   D   
0200   C3 0C 02               JMP   skipnx   
0203                DEF2:        
0203                          IF   CHECKED   
0203   7B                     MOV   A,E   
0204   FE DF                  CPI   " "-"A"+256   
0206   C2 26 06               JNZ   e_brack   ; anything but a letter or a space
0209                          ENDIF      
0209   E5                     PUSH   H   ; an anonymous block: push its address
020A   60                     MOV   H,B   
020B   69                     MOV   L,C   
020C                SKIPNX:      
020C                          IF   CHECKED   
020C   0B                     DCX   B   ; back onto the letter, so that skip finds its
020D                          ENDIF      ;   opener, the "[", just before where it starts
020D   CD 7C 04     SKIPO:    CALL   skip   
0210                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
0210                          DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
0210   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
0211   36                     DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
0212   01                     DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
0213   5E           H_FETCH:   MOV   E,M   ; "@"
0214   23                     INX   H   
0215   56                     MOV   D,M   
0216   EB                     XCHG      
0217                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
0217                          DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
0217   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
0218   36                     DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
0219   01                     DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
021A                             ; =============================================================================
021A                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's second page.
021A                             ;  "?" is the last (with "," inside it in the unchecked build), so its long
021A                             ;  tail may run past that page.
021A                             ; =============================================================================
021A                             ; ---- flow control ----------------------------------------------------------
021A                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
021A                             ; the matching ")".
021A   7C           H_OPEN:   MOV   A,H   
021B   B5                     ORA   L   
021C   E1                     POP   H   
021D   CA 0D 02               JZ   skipo   
0220   E5                     PUSH   H   ; (rpushd pops it again)
0221   50                     MOV   D,B   
0222   59                     MOV   E,C   ; the block starts at the IP
0223   C3 3B 05               JMP   rpushd   
0226                             ; ")" ( flag -- ): true jumps back to the block start (and keeps it); false
0226                             ; drops it and carries on.
0226   7C           H_CLOSE:   MOV   A,H   
0227   B5                     ORA   L   
0228   CA 06 01               JZ   rdrop   
022B                          ;*Macro unroll:  POPR                    ; pop the block start ...
022B                          DS   1-CPM,0CFh   ; pop the block start ...
022B   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
022C   0C                     DS   CPM,AROP&0FFh   
022D   01                     DS   CPM,AROP/256   
022E   44                     MOV   B,H   
022F   4D                     MOV   C,L   ; ... jump to it ...
0230   EB                     XCHG      
0231   C3 3B 05               JMP   rpushd   ; ... and push it back (which drops the flag)
0234                             ; ---- arithmetic and logic: ( NOS TOS -- result ) ---------------------------
0234                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
0234   0A           H_SUB:    LDAX   B   
0235   D6 30                  SUI   "0"   
0237   FE 0A                  CPI   10   
0239   DA 7E 03               JC   negnum   
023C                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEGH                    ; a - b = a + (-b): fall into '+'
023C                          DS   1-CPM,0E7h   ; a - b = a + (-b): fall into "+"
023C   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
023D   27                     DS   CPM,ANEG&0FFh   
023E   01                     DS   CPM,ANEG/256   
023F   D1           H_ADD:    POP   D   
0240   19                     DAD   D   
0241                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
0241                          DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
0241   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
0242   36                     DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
0243   01                     DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
0244   D1           H_AND:    POP   D   
0245   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0246   A2                     ANA   D   
0247   67                     MOV   H,A   
0248   7D                     MOV   A,L   
0249   A3                     ANA   E   
024A   6F                     MOV   L,A   
024B                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
024B                          DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
024B   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
024C   36                     DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
024D   01                     DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
024E                             ; Signed compares. Both are "DE < HL" for the right pair: > swaps the two
024E                             ; cells first (XTHL), < doesn't. There is no overflow flag, so the signed
024E                             ; answer is the unsigned borrow of DE - HL, flipped when the signs differ.
024E                             ; SBB A turns a carry into -1 or 0 with no branch.
024E   E3           H_GT:     XTHL      ; a > b  is  b < a
024F   D1           H_LT:     POP   D   ; a < b: DE = a, HL = b
0250   7B                     MOV   A,E   
0251   95                     SUB   L   
0252   7A                     MOV   A,D   
0253   9C                     SBB   H   
0254   9F                     SBB   A   ; A = -1 if DE < HL unsigned
0255   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0256   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0257   AA                     XRA   D   
0258   17                     RAL      ; carry = the signs differ
0259   9F                     SBB   A   
025A   AD                     XRA   L   ; flip when they do
025B   67                     MOV   H,A   
025C   6F                     MOV   L,A   
025D                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
025D                          DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
025D   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
025E   36                     DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
025F   01                     DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
0260   D1           H_EQ:     POP   D   
0261   7D                     MOV   A,L   
0262   AB                     XRA   E   
0263   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0264   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0265   AA                     XRA   D   
0266   B5                     ORA   L   ; zero if equal
0267   D6 01                  SUI   1   ; carry only for zero
0269   9F                     SBB   A   
026A   67                     MOV   H,A   
026B   6F                     MOV   L,A   
026C                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
026C                          DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
026C   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
026D   36                     DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
026E   01                     DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
026F                             ; "*": shift-and-add on the multiplier's low bit, so it stops as soon as the
026F                             ; multiplier is used up; only the low 16 bits are kept.
026F   D1           H_MUL:    POP   D   ; DE = multiplicand
0270   C5                     PUSH   B   
0271   44                     MOV   B,H   
0272   4D                     MOV   C,L   ; BC = multiplier
0273   21 00 00               LXI   H,0   
0276   78           MUL1:     MOV   A,B   
0277   B7                     ORA   A   ; clear carry
0278   1F                     RAR      
0279   47                     MOV   B,A   
027A   79                     MOV   A,C   
027B   1F                     RAR      
027C   4F                     MOV   C,A   ; BC >> 1, carry = the bit shifted out
027D   D2 81 02               JNC   mul2   
0280   19                     DAD   D   
0281   EB           MUL2:     XCHG      
0282   29                     DAD   H   ; multiplicand << 1
0283   EB                     XCHG      
0284   78                     MOV   A,B   
0285   B1                     ORA   C   
0286   C2 76 02               JNZ   mul1   
0289   C1                     POP   B   
028A                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
028A                          DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
028A   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
028B   36                     DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
028C   01                     DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
028D                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
028D                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
028D                             ; of a. Dividing by zero returns two cells of no meaning; the checked build
028D                             ; stops on it.
028D                H_DIV:       
028D                          IF   CHECKED   
028D   7C                     MOV   A,H   
028E   B5                     ORA   L   
028F   CA 23 06               JZ   e_zero   
0292                          ENDIF      
0292   D1                     POP   D   ; DE = a, HL = b
0293   C5                     PUSH   B   
0294   7A                     MOV   A,D   
0295   B7                     ORA   A   
0296   F5                     PUSH   PSW   ; S flag = sign of a (for r)
0297   AC                     XRA   H   
0298   F5                     PUSH   PSW   ; S flag = sign of q
0299   7C                     MOV   A,H   
029A   B7                     ORA   A   
029B   FC 27 01               CM   neg16   ; HL = |b|
029E   EB                     XCHG      
029F   7C                     MOV   A,H   
02A0   B7                     ORA   A   
02A1   FC 27 01               CM   neg16   ; HL = |a|, DE = |b|
02A4   CD 9F 03               CALL   udiv   ; HL = q, BC = r
02A7   F1                     POP   PSW   
02A8   FC 27 01               CM   neg16   ; q's sign
02AB   EB                     XCHG      ; DE = q
02AC   60                     MOV   H,B   
02AD   69                     MOV   L,C   ; HL = r
02AE   F1                     POP   PSW   
02AF   FC 27 01               CM   neg16   ; r's sign
02B2   C1                     POP   B   
02B3   D5                     PUSH   D   ; q under r
02B4                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
02B4                          DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
02B4   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
02B5   36                     DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
02B6   01                     DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
02B7                             ; ---- stack and storage -----------------------------------------------------
02B7   E5           H_DUP:    PUSH   H   ; ":"
02B8                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
02B8                          DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
02B8   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
02B9   36                     DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
02BA   01                     DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
02BB   E3           H_SWAP:   XTHL      ; "%"
02BC                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
02BC                          DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
02BC   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
02BD   36                     DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
02BE   01                     DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
02BF                             ; (The checked build tests the address before it takes the value off the
02BF                             ; stack, so that an error report shows both.)
02BF                H_STORE:      ; "!" ( n addr -- )
02BF                          IF   CHECKED   
02BF   CD 80 05               CALL   chkst   
02C2                          ENDIF      
02C2   D1                     POP   D   
02C3   73                     MOV   M,E   
02C4   23                     INX   H   
02C5   72                     MOV   M,D   
02C6                          ;*Macro unroll:  DROP
02C6                          DS   1-CPM,0DFh   
02C6   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
02C7   1C                     DS   CPM,ADRP&0FFh   
02C8   01                     DS   CPM,ADRP/256   
02C9                H_CSTORE:      ; "." ( c addr -- )
02C9                          IF   CHECKED   
02C9   CD 80 05               CALL   chkst   
02CC                          ENDIF      
02CC   D1                     POP   D   
02CD   73                     MOV   M,E   
02CE                          ;*Macro unroll:  DROP
02CE                          DS   1-CPM,0DFh   
02CE   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
02CF   1C                     DS   CPM,ADRP&0FFh   
02D0   01                     DS   CPM,ADRP/256   
02D1                             ; ---- console ---------------------------------------------------------------
02D1                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
02D1   E5           H_STR:    PUSH   H   
02D2   60                     MOV   H,B   
02D3   69                     MOV   L,C   
02D4   CD C0 04               CALL   skipstr   
02D7                          IF   CHECKED   
02D7   B7                     ORA   A   ; 0: the text ran out before the closing quote
02D8   CA 1B 06               JZ   e_quote   
02DB                          ENDIF      
02DB                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
02DB                          DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
02DB   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
02DC   36                     DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
02DD   01                     DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
02DE                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character from
02DE                             ; 60h to 7Eh is one of the escapes at pesc; "/" plus any other character
02DE                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, and / then DEL gives "?"; "/',
02DE                             ; '"' and '?' have no bit 6, so //, /" and /? give themselves).
02DE                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    H_PRINT:   JMP   prlp   ; (the loop is with the escapes, out of the
                    PRLOOP:   EQU   prlp   ;   way of the handlers, which must fit in
                    PRAGAIN:   EQU   prlp   ;   the image's first two pages)
02DE                          ENDIF      
02DE                          IF   CHECKED   
02DE                             ; (The checked build has the loop as a routine, prstr, which the error
02DE                             ; report uses too. The address is kept meanwhile, for a report: it shows
02DE                             ; the stack as it was before the "$". /~ comes back to hp1.)
02DE   22 3A 0A     H_PRINT:   SHLD   PSAVE   
02E1   CD 97 05     HP1:      CALL   prstr   
02E4                          ;*Macro unroll:  DROP
02E4                          DS   1-CPM,0DFh   
02E4   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
02E5   1C                     DS   CPM,ADRP&0FFh   
02E6   01                     DS   CPM,ADRP/256   
02E7                          ENDIF      
02E7   7D           H_EMIT:   MOV   A,L   ; "'"
02E8                          ;*Macro unroll:  PUTA
02E8                          DS   1-CPM,0EFh   
02E8   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
02E9   52                     DS   CPM,APUT&0FFh   
02EA   05                     DS   CPM,APUT/256   
02EB                          ;*Macro unroll: h_drop: DROP                    ; ';' is this one byte
02EB                H_DROP:   DS   1-CPM,0DFh   ; ";" is this one byte
02EB   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
02EC   1C                     DS   CPM,ADRP&0FFh   
02ED   01                     DS   CPM,ADRP/256   
02EE                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it.
02EE   C5           H_NUM:    PUSH   B   
02EF   CD D1 03               CALL   psgn   
02F2   C1                     POP   B   
02F3                          ;*Macro unroll:  DROP
02F3                          DS   1-CPM,0DFh   
02F3   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
02F4   1C                     DS   CPM,ADRP&0FFh   
02F5   01                     DS   CPM,ADRP/256   
02F6                          IF   CHECKED   ; (the checked build has no room to start ","
02F6   6E           H_CFETCH:   MOV   L,M   ;   as late as the unchecked one does: see
02F7   26 00                  MVI   H,0   ;   the end of "?")
02F9                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
02F9                          DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
02F9   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
02FA   36                     DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
02FB   01                     DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
02FC                          ENDIF      
02FC                             ; "?" ( n -- c ) or ( -n -- addr )
02FC                             ;   n > 0: wait about n ms for a key; 0 if none came
02FC                             ;   n = 0: wait for a key
02FC                             ;   n < 0: read a line of at most -n characters, with echo. The buffer
02FC                             ;          holds 127 characters and the CR: a bigger count is taken as 127.
02FC   7C           H_KEY:    MOV   A,H   
02FD   B7                     ORA   A   
02FE   FA 1E 03               JM   line   
0301   1E 04        KT1:      MVI   E,MSLOOP   ; one millisecond, roughly
0303   CD 18 05     KT2:      CALL   getk   
0306   C2 18 03               JNZ   kt3   
0309   1D                     DCR   E   
030A   C2 03 03               JNZ   kt2   
030D   7C                     MOV   A,H   ; 0? never counts down: it waits
030E   B5                     ORA   L   
030F   CA 01 03               JZ   kt1   
0312   2B                     DCX   H   
0313   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0314   B5                     ORA   L   
0315   C2 01 03               JNZ   kt1   ; A = 0 if the time ran out
0318                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              DB   0FEh   ; (CPI: steps over the one byte of ",")
                    H_CFETCH:   MOV   A,M   ; "," shares "?"s ending: A becomes TOS
0318                          ENDIF      
0318   6F           KT3:      MOV   L,A   
0319   26 00                  MVI   H,0   
031B                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
031B                          DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
031B   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
031C   36                     DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
031D   01                     DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
031E                             ; Backspace takes the last character back (and is echoed as
031E                             ; it is), CR ends (stored, not echoed), every other key is stored and
031E                             ; echoed until the line is full. The line buffer starts at offset 80h
031E                             ; of its page, so L alone is the place in the line: D holds the L of
031E                             ; a full line.
031E   11 7F 00     LINE:     LXI   D,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
0321   19                     DAD   D   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
0322   9F                     SBB   A   
0323   A5                     ANA   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
0324   2F                     CMA      
0325   57                     MOV   D,A   ; D = the L of a full line: 80h + count, FFh
0326                             ;   at most
0326   21 80 0A               LXI   H,LINEBUF   
0329   CD 18 05     LN2:      CALL   getk   
032C   CA 29 03               JZ   ln2   
032F   FE 0D                  CPI   13   
0331   CA 50 03               JZ   ln5   
0334   FE 08                  CPI   8   
0336   CA 48 03               JZ   ln4   
0339   5F                     MOV   E,A   
033A   7D                     MOV   A,L   
033B   BA                     CMP   D   
033C   CA 29 03               JZ   ln2   ; full
033F   73                     MOV   M,E   
0340   2C                     INR   L   
0341   7B                     MOV   A,E   
0342                          ;*Macro unroll: ln3:    PUTA
0342                LN3:      DS   1-CPM,0EFh   
0342   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
0343   52                     DS   CPM,APUT&0FFh   
0344   05                     DS   CPM,APUT/256   
0345   C3 29 03               JMP   ln2   
0348   2D           LN4:      DCR   L   ; Backspace: one back, and echo it,
0349   FA 42 03               JM   ln3   ;   unless the line was empty (L left the
034C   2C                     INR   L   ;   upper half of the page)
034D   C3 29 03               JMP   ln2   
0350   77           LN5:      MOV   M,A   ; the CR
0351   2E 80                  MVI   L,LINEBUF & 0FFh   
0353                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
0353                          DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
0353   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
0354   36                     DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
0355   01                     DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
0356                             ; =============================================================================
0356                             ;  Dispatch table: the low byte of each handler's address, in code order.
0356                             ;  It must not cross a page (the dispatcher only adds to its low byte).
0356                             ; =============================================================================
0356                             ; The handlers of the first NPG1 characters start in the image's second page.
0356                             ; ] \ [ @ sit where the two pages meet, and which side each lands on
0356                             ; differs between the builds, so the count is worked out here.
0356                             ; (One division to a line: asm80 only rounds down when it stores a value.)
0356                PGRET:    EQU   (h_ret-BASE)/256   ; 0 = first page, 1 = second
0356                PGBRK:    EQU   (h_break-BASE)/256   
0356                PGDEF:    EQU   (h_def-BASE)/256   
0356                PGFET:    EQU   (h_fetch-BASE)/256   
0356                NPG1:     EQU   21 + PGFET + PGDEF + PGBRK + PGRET   
0356   BF           PTAB:     DB   h_store & 0FFh   ; !
0357   D1                     DB   h_str & 0FFh   ; "
0358   EE                     DB   h_num & 0FFh   ; #
0359   DE                     DB   h_print & 0FFh   ; $
035A   BB                     DB   h_swap & 0FFh   ; %
035B   44                     DB   h_and & 0FFh   ; &
035C   E7                     DB   h_emit & 0FFh   ; '
035D   1A                     DB   h_open & 0FFh   ; (
035E   26                     DB   h_close & 0FFh   ; )
035F   6F                     DB   h_mul & 0FFh   ; *
0360   3F                     DB   h_add & 0FFh   ; +
0361   F6                     DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   ; ,
0362   34                     DB   h_sub & 0FFh   ; -
0363   C9                     DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   ; .
0364   8D                     DB   h_div & 0FFh   ; /
0365   B7                     DB   h_dup & 0FFh   ; :
0366   EB                     DB   h_drop & 0FFh   ; ;
0367   4F                     DB   h_lt & 0FFh   ; <
0368   60                     DB   h_eq & 0FFh   ; =
0369   4E                     DB   h_gt & 0FFh   ; >
036A   FC                     DB   h_key & 0FFh   ; ?
036B   13                     DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   ; @
036C   EA                     DB   h_def & 0FFh   ; [
036D   DB                     DB   h_break & 0FFh   ; \
036E   D2                     DB   h_ret & 0FFh   ; ]
036F   88                     DB   h_xor & 0FFh   ; ^
0370   A3                     DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   ; _
0371   B3                     DB   h_grave & 0FFh   ; `
0372   18                     DB   h_tor & 0FFh   ; {
0373   92                     DB   h_or & 0FFh   ; |
0374   20                     DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   ; }
0375   9C                     DB   h_not & 0FFh   ; ~
0376                PTABEND:      
0376                             ; =============================================================================
0376                             ;  Routines (no handler starts past this point)
0376                             ; =============================================================================
0376                             ; Digits: step back onto the first digit and read the whole number.
0376   E5           DIGIT:    PUSH   H   
0377   0B                     DCX   B   
0378   CD 88 03               CALL   rdnum   
037B                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
037B                          DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
037B   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
037C   36                     DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
037D   01                     DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
037E                             ; negnum: "-" directly before a digit: read the number, negate it.
037E   E5           NEGNUM:   PUSH   H   
037F   CD 88 03               CALL   rdnum   
0382                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEGH
0382                          DS   1-CPM,0E7h   
0382   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
0383   27                     DS   CPM,ANEG&0FFh   
0384   01                     DS   CPM,ANEG/256   
0385                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
0385                          DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
0385   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
0386   36                     DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
0387   01                     DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
0388                             ; rdnum: read decimal digits at IP into HL; IP is left on the first
0388                             ; non-digit. Values wrap at 16 bits, as the spec says.
0388   21 00 00     RDNUM:    LXI   H,0   
038B   0A           RDN1:     LDAX   B   
038C   D6 30                  SUI   "0"   
038E   FE 0A                  CPI   10   
0390   D0                     RNC      
0391   03                     INX   B   
0392   54                     MOV   D,H   
0393   5D                     MOV   E,L   
0394   29                     DAD   H   
0395   29                     DAD   H   
0396   19                     DAD   D   
0397   29                     DAD   H   ; HL * 10
0398   5F                     MOV   E,A   
0399   16 00                  MVI   D,0   
039B   19                     DAD   D   
039C   C3 8B 03               JMP   rdn1   
039F                             ; udiv: unsigned HL / DE (DE <= 8000h). Returns HL = quotient, BC = remainder.
039F                             ; Uses A, BC; the caller saves the IP. HL holds the dividend and, as its bits
039F                             ; leave at the top, the quotient bits arrive at the bottom. The loop counter
039F                             ; lives on the stack, since A is busy with the shifts.
039F                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
039F   01 00 00     UDIV:     LXI   B,0   
03A2   7B                     MOV   A,E   
03A3   EE 02                  XRI   2   
03A5   B2                     ORA   D   
03A6   C2 B3 03               JNZ   udv0   
03A9   B4                     ORA   H   ; A was 0, and the carry is clear
03AA   1F                     RAR      
03AB   67                     MOV   H,A   
03AC   7D                     MOV   A,L   
03AD   1F                     RAR      
03AE   6F                     MOV   L,A   ; the quotient
03AF   78                     MOV   A,B   
03B0   17                     RAL      
03B1   4F                     MOV   C,A   ; the remainder: the bit that fell out
03B2   C9                     RET      
03B3   3E 10        UDV0:     MVI   A,16   
03B5   F5                     PUSH   PSW   
03B6   29           UDV1:     DAD   H   ; next dividend bit into the carry
03B7   79                     MOV   A,C   
03B8   17                     RAL      
03B9   4F                     MOV   C,A   
03BA   78                     MOV   A,B   
03BB   17                     RAL      
03BC   47                     MOV   B,A   ; BC = BC*2 + bit
03BD   79                     MOV   A,C   
03BE   93                     SUB   E   
03BF   78                     MOV   A,B   
03C0   9A                     SBB   D   ; carry if BC < DE
03C1   DA C9 03               JC   udv2   
03C4   47                     MOV   B,A   ; BC - DE (high byte; A holds it)
03C5   79                     MOV   A,C   
03C6   93                     SUB   E   
03C7   4F                     MOV   C,A   
03C8   2C                     INR   L   ; quotient bit
03C9   F1           UDV2:     POP   PSW   
03CA   3D                     DCR   A   
03CB   F5                     PUSH   PSW   
03CC   C2 B6 03               JNZ   udv1   
03CF   F1                     POP   PSW   
03D0   C9                     RET      
03D1                             ; psgn: print HL as a signed number. Uses BC.
03D1   7C           PSGN:     MOV   A,H   
03D2   B7                     ORA   A   
03D3   F2 DE 03               JP   pdec   
03D6   3E 2D                  MVI   A,"-"   
03D8                          ;*Macro unroll:  PUTA
03D8                          DS   1-CPM,0EFh   
03D8   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
03D9   52                     DS   CPM,APUT&0FFh   
03DA   05                     DS   CPM,APUT/256   
03DB                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEGH
03DB                          DS   1-CPM,0E7h   
03DB   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
03DC   27                     DS   CPM,ANEG&0FFh   
03DD   01                     DS   CPM,ANEG/256   
03DE                             ; pdec: print HL unsigned, by recursion on HL / 10 (the stack holds digits).
03DE                             ; Uses BC.
03DE   11 0A 00     PDEC:     LXI   D,10   
03E1   CD 9F 03               CALL   udiv   ; HL = HL / 10, C = the last digit
03E4   79                     MOV   A,C   
03E5   F5                     PUSH   PSW   
03E6   7C                     MOV   A,H   
03E7   B5                     ORA   L   
03E8   C4 DE 03               CNZ   pdec   
03EB   F1                     POP   PSW   
03EC   C6 30                  ADI   "0"   
03EE                          ;*Macro unroll:  PUTA
03EE                          DS   1-CPM,0EFh   
03EE   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
03EF   52                     DS   CPM,APUT&0FFh   
03F0   05                     DS   CPM,APUT/256   
03F1   C9                     RET      
03F2                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                                 ; "$" prints the string at TOS (see h_print).
                    PRLP:     MOV   A,M   
                              INX   H   
                              CPI   22h   
                              JZ   h_drop   
                              CPI   "/"   
                              JNZ   pr1   
                              MOV   A,M   
                              INX   H   
                              CPI   60h   
                              JC   pr0   
                              CPI   7Fh   
                              JC   pesc   
                    PR0:      ANI   0BFh   
                              ;*Macro unroll: pr1:    PUTA
                    PR1:      DS   1-CPM,0EFh   
                              DS   CPM,0CDh   
                              DS   CPM,APUT&0FFh   
                              DS   CPM,APUT/256   
                              JMP   prlp   
03F2                          ENDIF      
03F2                             ;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
03F2                             ; pesc: the escapes of "$". A = the character after the "/", 60h to 7Eh, and
03F2                             ; HL points past it. Each goes back into the loop that prints the string
03F2                             ; (PRLOOP), but /~ has the stack to see to, and goes back by PRAGAIN.
03F2                             ;    /a-/z   print the variable, as "#" does
03F2                             ;    /{      clear the screen, the cursor to the top left
03F2                             ;    /}      clear from the cursor to the end of the line
03F2                             ;    /|  /`  show the cursor, hide it
03F2                             ;    /~      ( row col -- ) the cursor to that row and column, from 0
03F2   FE 7E        PESC:     CPI   7Eh   
03F4   CA 17 04               JZ   pat   
03F7   11 97 05               LXI   D,PRLOOP   ; the others return into the loop
03FA   D5                     PUSH   D   
03FB   D6 7B                  SUI   7Bh   ; 00bbIDAsIHwgMSwg 2, and no borrow
03FD   D2 58 04               JNC   pcon   
0400   C6 1A                  ADI   1Ah   ; a-z: 0-25, and a carry; `: FFh, and none
0402   D2 42 04               JNC   phide   
0405   87                     ADD   A   ; the variable's cell
0406   C6 40                  ADI   40h   
0408   E5                     PUSH   H   
0409   C5                     PUSH   B   
040A   6F                     MOV   L,A   
040B   26 0A                  MVI   H,LETPAGE   
040D   7E                     MOV   A,M   
040E   2C                     INR   L   
040F   66                     MOV   H,M   
0410   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0411   CD D1 03               CALL   psgn   
0414   C1                     POP   B   
0415   E1                     POP   H   
0416   C9                     RET      
0417                             ; /~ ( row col addr -- ): the two cells under the string's address go. In
0417                             ; the checked build "$" is the routine prstr: its own return address goes
0417                             ; first, and hp1 calls it again afterwards. There each /~ first looks that
0417                             ; its two cells are there, and is s if not, before it prints anything.
0417                PAT:         
0417                          IF   CHECKED   
0417   E3                     XTHL      ; the text pointer over prstr's return address
0418   21 0A F6               LXI   H,(6-DSTOP)&0FFFFh   ; a carry: the two cells aren't there
041B   39                     DAD   SP   
041C   DA F8 05               JC   e_under   
041F   E1                     POP   H   
0420                          ENDIF      
0420   D1                     POP   D   ; DE = the column
0421   E3                     XTHL      ; HL = the row; the text pointer is kept
0422                          IF   1-ANS   
                              CALL   CONAT   
                              POP   H   
                              JMP   PRAGAIN   
                                 ; With ANSI = 0 the machine's routines do the rest.
                    PCON:     JZ   CONCLS   ; /{
                              CPI   2   
                              JZ   CONEOL   ; /}
                              DB   0FEh   ; /|  (CPI steps over the XRA: A = 1, show)
                    PHIDE:    XRA   A   ; /`  (A = 0: hide)
                              JMP   CONCUR   
0422                          ENDIF      
0422                          IF   ANS   
0422   C5                     PUSH   B   ; (pdec uses BC)
0423   D5                     PUSH   D   
0424   CD 71 04               CALL   csi   ; ESC [ row+1 ; col+1 H (ANSI counts from 1)
0427   23                     INX   H   
0428   CD DE 03               CALL   pdec   
042B   3E 3B                  MVI   A,";"   
042D                          ;*Macro unroll:  PUTA
042D                          DS   1-CPM,0EFh   
042D   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
042E   52                     DS   CPM,APUT&0FFh   
042F   05                     DS   CPM,APUT/256   
0430   E1                     POP   H   
0431   23                     INX   H   
0432   CD DE 03               CALL   pdec   
0435   3E 48                  MVI   A,"H"   
0437                          ;*Macro unroll:  PUTA
0437                          DS   1-CPM,0EFh   
0437   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
0438   52                     DS   CPM,APUT&0FFh   
0439   05                     DS   CPM,APUT/256   
043A   C1                     POP   B   
043B   E1                     POP   H   
043C   C3 E1 02               JMP   PRAGAIN   
043F                             ; With ANSI = 1 they are sequences. The carry is clear on the way in.
043F   1E 68        PSHOW:    MVI   E,"h"   ; /|  ESC [ ? 2 5 h
0441   DA                     DB   0DAh   ; (JC nn: with no carry it steps over two bytes)
0442   1E 6C        PHIDE:    MVI   E,"l"   ; /`  ESC [ ? 2 5 l
0444   3E 3F                  MVI   A,"?"   
0446   CD 68 04               CALL   csia   
0449   3E 32                  MVI   A,"2"   
044B                          ;*Macro unroll:  PUTA
044B                          DS   1-CPM,0EFh   
044B   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
044C   52                     DS   CPM,APUT&0FFh   
044D   05                     DS   CPM,APUT/256   
044E   3E 35                  MVI   A,"5"   
0450                          ;*Macro unroll:  PUTA
0450                          DS   1-CPM,0EFh   
0450   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
0451   52                     DS   CPM,APUT&0FFh   
0452   05                     DS   CPM,APUT/256   
0453   7B                     MOV   A,E   
0454                          ;*Macro unroll:  PUTA
0454                          DS   1-CPM,0EFh   
0454   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
0455   52                     DS   CPM,APUT&0FFh   
0456   05                     DS   CPM,APUT/256   
0457   C9                     RET      
0458                             ; pcon: /00bbIC98IC8=, with A = 0, 1, 2. /{ runs on into csia.
0458   3D           PCON:     DCR   A   
0459   CA 3F 04               JZ   pshow   ; /|
045C   3E 4B                  MVI   A,"K"   
045E   F2 68 04               JP   csia   ; /}  ESC [ K
0461   3E 48                  MVI   A,"H"   ; /{  ESC [ H ESC [ J
0463   CD 68 04               CALL   csia   
0466   3E 4A                  MVI   A,"J"   ; (on into csia)
0468                             ; csia: ESC [ and then A. csi: ESC [. Both keep all but A.
0468   F5           CSIA:     PUSH   PSW   
0469   CD 71 04               CALL   csi   
046C   F1                     POP   PSW   
046D                          ;*Macro unroll:  PUTA
046D                          DS   1-CPM,0EFh   
046D   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
046E   52                     DS   CPM,APUT&0FFh   
046F   05                     DS   CPM,APUT/256   
0470   C9                     RET      
0471   3E 1B        CSI:      MVI   A,27   
0473                          ;*Macro unroll:  PUTA
0473                          DS   1-CPM,0EFh   
0473   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
0474   52                     DS   CPM,APUT&0FFh   
0475   05                     DS   CPM,APUT/256   
0476   3E 5B                  MVI   A,"["   
0478                          ;*Macro unroll:  PUTA
0478                          DS   1-CPM,0EFh   
0478   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
0479   52                     DS   CPM,APUT&0FFh   
047A   05                     DS   CPM,APUT/256   
047B   C9                     RET      
047C                          ENDIF      
047C                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return A = 0 if it
047C                             ; was ")" and 2 if it was "]". Brackets of both kinds count together;
047C                             ; strings are stepped over whole. A NUL first ends the program (for "\" with
047C                             ; no closer; anything else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets
047C                             ; anyway). D counts the open levels, starting at 1 for the one we are in:
047C                             ; skip sets it to 0 and falls through the INR that an opener comes back to.
047C                             ; 
047C                             ; The checked build also looks at the character the skip was started by,
047C                             ; which is always the one just before where it starts: "(" must end at ")",
047C                             ; "[" at "]", and neither may run into the NUL (N); a string with no closing
047C                             ; quote counts as running into it. "\" takes either closer. The place where
047C                             ; the skip started is kept on the stack, for the report.
047C                SKIP:        
047C                          IF   CHECKED   
047C   C5                     PUSH   B   
047D   0B                     DCX   B   
047E   0A                     LDAX   B   
047F   03                     INX   B   
0480   5F                     MOV   E,A   ; E = the opener: ( [ or \
0481                          ENDIF      
0481   16 00                  MVI   D,0   
0483   14           SK3:      INR   D   ; an opener: one deeper
0484   0A           SK1:      LDAX   B   
0485                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              INX   B   
                              ORA   A   
                              JZ   endprog   
0485                          ENDIF      
0485                          IF   CHECKED   
0485   B7                     ORA   A   
0486   CA B4 04               JZ   sk6   ; (the IP stays on the NUL)
0489   03                     INX   B   
048A                          ENDIF      
048A   FE 22                  CPI   22h   
048C   CC C0 04               CZ   skipstr   ; leaves A = 22h, which matches nothing below
048F   D6 28                  SUI   "("   ;   (or 0, and then the NUL is read next)
0491   CA 83 04               JZ   sk3   
0494   3D                     DCR   A   ; ")"
0495   CA A2 04               JZ   sk4   
0498   D6 32                  SUI   "["-")"   
049A   CA 83 04               JZ   sk3   
049D   FE 02                  CPI   "]"-"["   
049F   C2 84 04               JNZ   sk1   
04A2   15           SK4:      DCR   D   
04A3                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              RZ      ; the closer at this level
                              JMP   sk1   
04A3                          ENDIF      
04A3                          IF   CHECKED   
04A3   C2 84 04               JNZ   sk1   
04A6   57                     MOV   D,A   ; the closer at this level: 0 or 2. Bit 1 of the
04A7   AB                     XRA   E   ;   opener is 0 for "(" and 1 for "[", and only
04A8   E6 06                  ANI   6   ;   "\" has bit 2: so this is 2 for the wrong
04AA   FE 02                  CPI   2   ;   closer, and only then
04AC   7A                     MOV   A,D   
04AD   D1                     POP   D   ; (where the skip started)
04AE   C0                     RNZ      
04AF   42                     MOV   B,D   ; N. The place is the opener
04B0   4B                     MOV   C,E   
04B1   C3 BB 04               JMP   sk7   
04B4   7B           SK6:      MOV   A,E   ; the text ran out:
04B5   E6 04                  ANI   4   
04B7   C2 85 01               JNZ   endprog   ;   "\" with no closer ends the program
04BA   C1                     POP   B   
04BB   3E 4E        SK7:      MVI   A,"N"   
04BD   C3 29 06               JMP   errp   ; (errp drops skip's return address)
04C0                          ENDIF      
04C0                             ; skipstr: IP is inside a string; step past its closing quote. "/" escapes
04C0                             ; the next character, so "/"" does not end it. Leaves A = 22h.
04C0                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    SS0:      INX   B   
                    SKIPSTR:   LDAX   B   
                              INX   B   
                              CPI   "/"   
                              JZ   ss0   
                              CPI   22h   
                              JNZ   skipstr   
                              RET      
04C0                          ENDIF      
04C0                          IF   CHECKED   
04C0                             ; The checked build never steps over a NUL: if the text runs out first it
04C0                             ; returns A = 0 with the IP on the NUL.
04C0   0A           SKIPSTR:   LDAX   B   
04C1   B7                     ORA   A   
04C2   C8                     RZ      
04C3   03                     INX   B   
04C4   FE 22                  CPI   22h   
04C6   C8                     RZ      
04C7   FE 2F                  CPI   "/"   
04C9   C2 C0 04               JNZ   skipstr   
04CC   0A                     LDAX   B   ; the escaped character
04CD   B7                     ORA   A   
04CE   C8                     RZ      
04CF   03                     INX   B   
04D0   C3 C0 04               JMP   skipstr   
04D3                          ENDIF      
04D3                             ; hexc: if the character at IP is a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), step over it
04D3                             ; and return its value in A with the carry set; otherwise leave the IP and
04D3                             ; return with the carry clear.
04D3   0A           HEXC:     LDAX   B   
04D4   D6 30                  SUI   "0"   
04D6   FE 0A                  CPI   10   
04D8   DA E4 04               JC   hc1   
04DB   E6 DF                  ANI   0DFh   
04DD   D6 11                  SUI   11h   
04DF   FE 06                  CPI   6   
04E1   D0                     RNC      
04E2   D6 F6                  SUI   0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
04E4   03           HC1:      INX   B   
04E5   C9                     RET      
04E6                             ; =============================================================================
04E6                             ;  Console layer. rawk is the host's key routine: a waiting key in A (zero
04E6                             ;  flag clear), or A = 0 with the zero flag set when none is waiting. putc
04E6                             ;  (RST 5) prints A. Both keep BC, DE and HL. In the generic build they are
04E6                             ;  the host's KEY and CONOUT routines themselves.
04E6                             ; 
04E6                             ;  A running program reads the keyboard only through getk and pollk, which
04E6                             ;  between them give the break key its rules:
04E6                             ;    - Ctrl-C stops the program;
04E6                             ;    - any other key that the break check reads is held in KEYBUF for the
04E6                             ;      next "?", and a newer one takes its place;
04E6                             ;    - "?" (getk) takes the held key first;
04E6                             ;    - a program that has stored a non-zero byte at BRKOFF gets Ctrl-C as a
04E6                             ;      key like any other, but two of them within about 250 ms still stop it.
04E6                             ;  Both are called straight from a handler, never from a routine under one:
04E6                             ;  the checked build's report counts on finding one return address above the
04E6                             ;  data stack, and TOS in HL.
04E6                             ; =============================================================================
04E6                          IFN   CPM   
                    RAWK:     EQU   KEY   
04E6                          ENDIF      
04E6                             ; pollk: the break check (see rpushd).
04E6   CD 50 05     POLLK:    CALL   rawk   
04E9   C8                     RZ      ; no key
04EA   32 7A 0A               STA   KEYBUF   ; held for the next "?"
04ED   FE 03        PK1:      CPI   3   ; (getk joins here)
04EF   C0                     RNZ      
04F0                             ; ctlc: Ctrl-C has been read. If the break key is on, that is the end. If
04F0                             ; the program has turned it off, wait about 250 ms for one more key: a
04F0                             ; second Ctrl-C is the end too; any other key is held (the newest wins),
04F0                             ; and the Ctrl-C goes to the program: returns A = 3, zero flag clear.
04F0   3A 7B 0A     CTLC:     LDA   BRKOFF   
04F3   B7                     ORA   A   
04F4   CA 92 05               JZ   brk   
04F7   D5                     PUSH   D   
04F8   11 E8 03               LXI   D,250*MSLOOP   
04FB   CD 50 05     CT1:      CALL   rawk   
04FE   C2 07 05               JNZ   ct2   
0501   1B                     DCX   D   
0502   7A                     MOV   A,D   
0503   B3                     ORA   E   
0504   C2 FB 04               JNZ   ct1   
0507   D1           CT2:      POP   D   ; A = the second key, or 0 if none came
0508   FE 03                  CPI   3   
050A   CA 92 05               JZ   brk   
050D   B7                     ORA   A   
050E   CA 14 05               JZ   ct3   
0511   32 7A 0A               STA   KEYBUF   
0514   3E 03        CT3:      MVI   A,3   
0516   B7                     ORA   A   
0517   C9                     RET      
0518                             ; getk: a key for "?", or A = 0 and the zero flag if there is none.
0518   E5           GETK:     PUSH   H   ; a held key goes first, and is taken out of
0519   21 7A 0A               LXI   H,KEYBUF   ;   the buffer
051C   7E                     MOV   A,M   
051D   36 00                  MVI   M,0   
051F   E1                     POP   H   
0520   B7                     ORA   A   
0521   C0                     RNZ      
0522   CD 50 05               CALL   rawk   
0525   C8                     RZ      
0526   C3 ED 04               JMP   pk1   ; Ctrl-C? If not, that is the key
0529                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    BRK:      EQU   endprog   ; the unchecked build stops without a word;
0529                          ENDIF      
0529                          IF   CHECKED   
0529                BRK:      EQU   e_break   ;   the checked build reports B
0529                          ENDIF      
0529                          IF   CPM   
0529                             ; (In a CP/M build the letters and digits are here, out of the way of the
0529                             ; handlers, which must fit in the image's first two pages. The same code as
0529                             ; in the generic build.)
0529                             ; ---- the letters and digits --------------------------------------------------
0529                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
0529   E5           LOWER:    PUSH   H   
052A   87                     ADD   A   
052B   6F                     MOV   L,A   
052C   26 0A                  MVI   H,LETPAGE   
052E                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
052E                          DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
052E   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
052F   36                     DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
0530   01                     DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
0531                             ; A-Z: call the word. The return address (the IP after the letter) goes on
0531                             ; the return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
0531   E5           UPPER:    PUSH   H   ; keep TOS: rpushd pops it back
0532   87                     ADD   A   
0533   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0534   26 0A                  MVI   H,LETPAGE   ; HL -> cell
0536   50                     MOV   D,B   
0537   59                     MOV   E,C   ; DE = the return address
0538   4E                     MOV   C,M   
0539   23                     INX   H   
053A   46                     MOV   B,M   ; IP = the word's body, and fall into rpushd
053B                             ; rpushd: push DE on the return stack, then pop TOS off the data stack and
053B                             ; go on. Every push of the return stack ends here: for a word call the cell
053B                             ; popped is the TOS that upper parked; for "(" and "{" it is the cell under
053B                             ; the one that was used up.
053B                             ; 
053B                             ; The break key is looked at here, so at every word call and loop-back (and
053B                             ; block entry and "{"), but only one time in 256: BRKCNT counts them. Reading
053B                             ; the keyboard can be slow (it is a BDOS call under CP/M).
053B   2A 34 0A     RPUSHD:   LHLD   RSP   
053E   2B                     DCX   H   
053F   72                     MOV   M,D   
0540   2B                     DCX   H   
0541   73                     MOV   M,E   
0542   22 34 0A               SHLD   RSP   
0545   21 36 0A               LXI   H,BRKCNT   
0548   35                     DCR   M   
0549   E1                     POP   H   ; (keeps the flags)
054A   CC E6 04               CZ   pollk   
054D                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEXT
054D                          DS   1-CPM,0F7h   
054D   C3                     DS   CPM,0C3h   
054E   36                     DS   CPM,ANXT&0FFh   
054F   01                     DS   CPM,ANXT/256   
0550   3E FF        RAWK:     MVI   A,0FFh   ; BDOS 6 with E = FFh: a key, or 0
0552                             ; putc: BDOS 6 for every character. BDOS 2 would check for ^S while
0552                             ; printing and could swallow a key that BDOS 6 then never sees.
0552   C5           PUTC:     PUSH   B   
0553   D5                     PUSH   D   
0554   E5                     PUSH   H   
0555   5F                     MOV   E,A   
0556   0E 06                  MVI   C,6   
0558   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   
055B   E1                     POP   H   
055C   D1                     POP   D   
055D   C1                     POP   B   
055E   B7                     ORA   A   ; (for getk)
055F   C9                     RET      
0560                          ENDIF      
0560                             ; =============================================================================
0560                             ;  Checked build: the checks and the error report
0560                             ; =============================================================================
0560                          IF   CHECKED   
0560                             ; chkhp: HL = the new heap top, DE = the count, the carry is from adding
0560                             ; it, and the old top is on the stack under the return address. Stop if the
0560                             ; new top is not below the limit page, or is below the program's end.
0560                CHKHP:       
0560                          ENDIF      
0560                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
0560                             ; With this much room a top that wrapped round can land back in
0560                             ; range, so the add is tested too: growing must not carry, and
0560                             ; releasing must.
0560   7A                     MOV   A,D   
0561   1F                     RAR      ; the carry comes in above the count's sign:
0562   C6 40                  ADI   40h   ;   bit 7 = carry XOR sign
0564   87                     ADD   A   
0565   DA 79 05               JC   e_heap   
0568   3A 07 00               LDA   0007h   
056B   3D                     DCR   A   
056C   BC                     CMP   H   
056D   DA 79 05               JC   e_heap   
0570                          ENDIF      
0570                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
                                 ; (Here the program's space is under 32K, so a top that wrapped
                                 ; round always falls outside it.)
                              MOV   A,H   
                              CPI   HEAPLIM   
                              JNC   e_heap   
0570                          ENDIF      
0570                          IF   CHECKED   
0570   EB                     XCHG      
0571   E5                     PUSH   H   ; the count
0572   2A 38 0A               LHLD   NPEND   
0575   19                     DAD   D   ; carry: at or above the program's end
0576   E1                     POP   H   
0577   EB                     XCHG      
0578   D8                     RC      
0579   EB           E_HEAP:   XCHG      ; put the count back in TOS for the report,
057A   D1                     POP   D   ;   and drop the return address (errp drops
057B   3E 48                  MVI   A,"H"   ;   the old top)
057D   C3 29 06               JMP   errp   
0580                             ; chkst: stop unless HL is in the program's own space: from the letter page
0580                             ; up to the heap limit (the OS, or HEAPLIM), so the interpreter's stacks and
0580                             ; whatever lies above the limit are safe. Memory above the heap top but
0580                             ; below the limit is the program's own: Tiny BASIC keeps its lines there.
0580                             ; It is the page of HL + 1 that is tested, so that one test serves both
0580                             ; bytes of a cell: the last byte below the limit can"t be stored to with ".'.
0580                             ; Keeps HL and BC. It runs on into its own error entry.
0580   23           CHKST:    INX   H   
0581   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0582   2B                     DCX   H   
0583   FE 0A                  CPI   LETPAGE   
0585   DA 8F 05               JC   e_store   
0588                          ENDIF      
0588                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
                              CPI   HEAPLIM   
                              RC      
0588                          ENDIF      
0588                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
0588   5F                     MOV   E,A   
0589   3A 07 00               LDA   0007h   ; the BDOS page is the heap limit
058C   3D                     DCR   A   
058D   BB                     CMP   E   
058E   D0                     RNC      
058F                          ENDIF      
058F                          IF   CHECKED   
058F                             ; Two error entries for errors found inside a routine: the first hides the
058F                             ; second inside a 3-byte LXI D (the 11h); errp then drops the routine's
058F                             ; return address.
058F   3E 4F        E_STORE:   MVI   A,"O"   ; a store outside the program's space
0591   11                     DB   11h   
0592   3E 42        E_BREAK:   MVI   A,"B"   ; Ctrl-C (found inside pollk or getk)
0594   C3 29 06               JMP   errp   
0597                             ; prstr: print the string at HL, to its closing quote, decoding "/" (this is
0597                             ; "$", and the error report's texts). A NUL first is an error: Q.
0597   7E           PRSTR:    MOV   A,M   
0598   23                     INX   H   
0599   FE 22                  CPI   22h   
059B   C8                     RZ      
059C   B7                     ORA   A   
059D   CA 11 06               JZ   e_dollar   
05A0   FE 2F                  CPI   "/"   
05A2   C2 B3 05               JNZ   prs1   
05A5   7E                     MOV   A,M   
05A6   23                     INX   H   
05A7   FE 60                  CPI   60h   
05A9   DA B1 05               JC   prs0   
05AC   FE 7F                  CPI   7Fh   
05AE   DA F2 03               JC   pesc   
05B1   E6 BF        PRS0:     ANI   0BFh   
05B3                          ;*Macro unroll: prs1:   PUTA
05B3                PRS1:     DS   1-CPM,0EFh   
05B3   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
05B4   52                     DS   CPM,APUT&0FFh   
05B5   05                     DS   CPM,APUT/256   
05B6   C3 97 05               JMP   prstr   
05B9                PRLOOP:   EQU   prstr   ; (where the escapes go back to)
05B9                PRAGAIN:   EQU   hp1   ; (and where /~ goes back to)
05B9                             ; pmsg: print the text that follows the CALL, to its closing quote. Keeps HL.
05B9                             ; pnl: the same, on a new line.
05B9   3E 0D        PNL:      MVI   A,13   
05BB                          ;*Macro unroll:  PUTA
05BB                          DS   1-CPM,0EFh   
05BB   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
05BC   52                     DS   CPM,APUT&0FFh   
05BD   05                     DS   CPM,APUT/256   
05BE   3E 0A                  MVI   A,10   
05C0                          ;*Macro unroll:  PUTA
05C0                          DS   1-CPM,0EFh   
05C0   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
05C1   52                     DS   CPM,APUT&0FFh   
05C2   05                     DS   CPM,APUT/256   
05C3   E3           PMSG:     XTHL      
05C4   CD 97 05               CALL   prstr   
05C7   E3                     XTHL      
05C8   C9                     RET      
05C9                             ; chkstk: both stacks are checked once per character, not in every handler.
05C9                             ; The data stack is right when SP lies in the 256 bytes below DSTOP: adding
05C9                             ; the constant carries if it is above (cells were popped that were never
05C9                             ; pushed), and leaves a high byte of FFh if it is in range. Errors are found
05C9                             ; a character late at most: the bytes above DSTOP and the guard band below
05C9                             ; the page take what happens meanwhile.
05C9   EB           CHKSTK:   XCHG      ; DE = TOS (HL is needed for the pointers)
05CA   21 05 F6               LXI   H,(1-DSTOP)&0FFFFh   ; (SP is 2 lower here: the call)
05CD   39                     DAD   SP   
05CE   DA F8 05               JC   e_under   
05D1   24                     INR   H   
05D2   C2 F2 05               JNZ   e_over   
05D5   2A 34 0A               LHLD   RSP   ; the return stack: in its page (or it has
05D8   7C                     MOV   A,H   ;   overflowed), and not above its empty
05D9   FE 08                  CPI   RSPAGE   ;   position (an underflow stays inside the
05DB   C2 EF 05               JNZ   e_rover   ;   page, in the guard band)
05DE   7D                     MOV   A,L   
05DF   FE E1                  CPI   RSTOP&0FFh+1   
05E1   D2 E6 05               JNC   e_runder   
05E4   EB                     XCHG      ; TOS back
05E5   C9                     RET      
05E6   21 E0 08     E_RUNDER:   LXI   H,RSTOP   ; return stack underflow: it counts as empty
05E9   22 34 0A               SHLD   RSP   
05EC   3E 72                  MVI   A,"r"   
05EE   21                     DB   21h   ; (LXI H hides the next entry; HL is free)
05EF   3E 52        E_ROVER:   MVI   A,"R"   ; return stack overflow
05F1   21                     DB   21h   
05F2   3E 53        E_OVER:   MVI   A,"S"   ; data stack overflow
05F4   EB                     XCHG      ; TOS back
05F5   C3 29 06               JMP   errp   
05F8   31 FC 09     E_UNDER:   LXI   SP,DSTOP   ; data stack underflow: it counts as empty
05FB   3E 73                  MVI   A,"s"   
05FD   C3 2A 06               JMP   error   
0600                             ; e_hi: the inner loop read a reserved byte, 80h-FFh: X. But a word cell that
0600                             ; was never defined still holds 0000h, and the byte there is a JMP, C3h, in
0600                             ; every build: if the IP is in page zero, this was a call of an undefined
0600                             ; word. The call is undone, so the place is the call itself.
0600   04           E_HI:     INR   B   
0601   05                     DCR   B   
0602   C2 20 06               JNZ   e_resv   
0605   E5                     PUSH   H   
0606                          ;*Macro unroll:  POPR
0606                          DS   1-CPM,0CFh   
0606   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
0607   0C                     DS   CPM,AROP&0FFh   
0608   01                     DS   CPM,AROP/256   
0609   44                     MOV   B,H   
060A   4D                     MOV   C,L   
060B   E1                     POP   H   
060C   3E 55                  MVI   A,"U"   
060E   C3 2A 06               JMP   error   
0611                             ; e_dollar: "$" ran into a NUL (in prstr): Q, with the string's address
0611                             ; back in TOS. prstr"s return address goes first. But if "$' had no
0611                             ; address at all (the stack was empty), it is s, found now: chkstk, called
0611                             ; one cell up, sees the stack past its empty place then.
0611   D1           E_DOLLAR:   POP   D   
0612   E1                     POP   H   
0613   CD C9 05               CALL   chkstk   
0616   E5                     PUSH   H   
0617   2A 3A 0A               LHLD   PSAVE   
061A   11                     DB   11h   ; (LXI D hides e_quote's first two bytes)
061B                             ; Error entries. Each loads its letter and then hides the next entry inside
061B                             ; a 3-byte LXI D (the 11h), so they all fall through to `error`.
061B   44           E_QUOTE:   MOV   B,H   ; an unclosed string: HL is its address, one
061C   4D                     MOV   C,L   ;   past the opening quote, which is the place
061D   3E 51                  MVI   A,"Q"   
061F   11                     DB   11h   
0620   3E 58        E_RESV:   MVI   A,"X"   ; a reserved byte outside a string
0622   11                     DB   11h   
0623   3E 5A        E_ZERO:   MVI   A,"Z"   ; dividing by zero
0625   11                     DB   11h   
0626   3E 57        E_BRACK:   MVI   A,"W"   ; bad character after [
0628   FE                     DB   0FEh   ; (CPI hides the one byte of errp)
0629                             ; errp: an error found inside a routine: drop its return address first.
0629   D1           ERRP:     POP   D   
062A                             ; error: the report, then the end. A = the letter, BC = one past the place,
062A                             ; HL = TOS, and both stacks as the report is to show them:
062A                             ; 
062A                             ;   Err X @ line,col
062A                             ;   D:n: the top 8 cells at most, bottom to top
062A                             ;   R:n
062A   E5           ERROR:    PUSH   H   ; now the whole data stack is in memory
062B   5F                     MOV   E,A   
062C   CD B9 05               CALL   pnl   
062F   45 72 72 20 22         DB   "Err ",22h   
0634   7B                     MOV   A,E   
0635                          ;*Macro unroll:  PUTA
0635                          DS   1-CPM,0EFh   
0635   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
0636   52                     DS   CPM,APUT&0FFh   
0637   05                     DS   CPM,APUT/256   
0638   CD C3 05               CALL   pmsg   
063B   20 40 20 22            DB   " @ ",22h   
063F   0B                     DCX   B   ; BC = the place
0640                             ; The line and column. A place below the program is in the line
0640                             ; buffer: line 0. Otherwise count the LFs from the program's start;
0640                             ; DE = the line's number, HL = where it starts.
0640   21 80 0A               LXI   H,LINEBUF   
0643   11 00 00               LXI   D,0   
0646   78                     MOV   A,B   
0647   FE 0B                  CPI   PROG/256   
0649   DA 63 06               JC   er3   
064C   24                     INR   H   
064D   6B                     MOV   L,E   ; HL = PROG
064E   13           ER1:      INX   D   ; a new line starts at HL
064F   E5                     PUSH   H   
0650   7D           ER2:      MOV   A,L   
0651   91                     SUB   C   
0652   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0653   98                     SBB   B   
0654   D2 62 06               JNC   er2x   ; reached the place
0657   7E                     MOV   A,M   
0658   23                     INX   H   
0659   FE 0A                  CPI   10   
065B   C2 50 06               JNZ   er2   
065E   F1                     POP   PSW   
065F   C3 4E 06               JMP   er1   
0662   E1           ER2X:     POP   H   
0663   C5           ER3:      PUSH   B   
0664   E5                     PUSH   H   
0665   EB                     XCHG      
0666   CD DE 03               CALL   pdec   ; the line
0669   3E 2C                  MVI   A,","   
066B                          ;*Macro unroll:  PUTA
066B                          DS   1-CPM,0EFh   
066B   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
066C   52                     DS   CPM,APUT&0FFh   
066D   05                     DS   CPM,APUT/256   
066E   D1                     POP   D   
066F   E1                     POP   H   
0670   CD E1 06               CALL   sub16   
0673   23                     INX   H   
0674   CD DE 03               CALL   pdec   ; the column
0677   CD B9 05               CALL   pnl   
067A   44 3A 22               DB   "D:",22h   
067D   21 06 F6               LXI   H,(2-DSTOP)&0FFFFh   ; SP - (DSTOP-2) is minus twice the depth
0680   39                     DAD   SP   ;   (the cell at DSTOP-2 was pushed with the
0681                          ;*Macro unroll:  NEGH                    ;   first value and holds nothing)
0681                          DS   1-CPM,0E7h   ;   first value and holds nothing)
0681   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
0682   27                     DS   CPM,ANEG&0FFh   
0683   01                     DS   CPM,ANEG/256   
0684   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0685   CD D5 06               CALL   phal2   ; the depth
0688   3E 3A                  MVI   A,":"   
068A                          ;*Macro unroll:  PUTA
068A                          DS   1-CPM,0EFh   
068A   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
068B   52                     DS   CPM,APUT&0FFh   
068C   05                     DS   CPM,APUT/256   
068D   79                     MOV   A,C   
068E   FE 09                  CPI   9   
0690   DA 9D 06               JC   er6   
0693   CD C3 05               CALL   pmsg   
0696   20 2E 2E 2E 22         DB   " ...",22h   
069B   0E 08                  MVI   C,8   
069D   26 00        ER6:      MVI   H,0   ; C = the number of cells to show
069F   69                     MOV   L,C   
06A0   29                     DAD   H   
06A1   39                     DAD   SP   ; HL -> just above the deepest of them
06A2   0C                     INR   C   
06A3   0D           ER7:      DCR   C   
06A4   CA BB 06               JZ   er8   
06A7   2B                     DCX   H   
06A8   56                     MOV   D,M   
06A9   2B                     DCX   H   
06AA   5E                     MOV   E,M   
06AB   E5                     PUSH   H   
06AC   C5                     PUSH   B   
06AD   3E 20                  MVI   A," "   
06AF                          ;*Macro unroll:  PUTA
06AF                          DS   1-CPM,0EFh   
06AF   CD                     DS   CPM,0CDh   
06B0   52                     DS   CPM,APUT&0FFh   
06B1   05                     DS   CPM,APUT/256   
06B2   EB                     XCHG      
06B3   CD D1 03               CALL   psgn   
06B6   C1                     POP   B   
06B7   E1                     POP   H   
06B8   C3 A3 06               JMP   er7   
06BB   CD B9 05     ER8:      CALL   pnl   
06BE   52 3A 22               DB   "R:",22h   
06C1   2A 34 0A               LHLD   RSP   
06C4   EB                     XCHG      
06C5   21 E0 08               LXI   H,RSTOP   
06C8   CD D2 06               CALL   phalf   
06CB   CD B9 05               CALL   pnl   
06CE   22                     DB   22h   
06CF   C3 85 01               JMP   endprog   
06D2                             ; phalf: print half of HL - DE, and leave it in BC
06D2   CD E1 06     PHALF:    CALL   sub16   
06D5   B7           PHAL2:    ORA   A   ; (A = H; this clears the carry)
06D6   1F                     RAR      
06D7   67                     MOV   H,A   
06D8   7D                     MOV   A,L   
06D9   1F                     RAR      
06DA   6F                     MOV   L,A   
06DB   E5                     PUSH   H   
06DC   CD DE 03               CALL   pdec   
06DF   C1                     POP   B   
